## §9 — Condense
**Pattern (the wave's headline, §9 rule fired):** Amendment A13 — landed last cycle precisely to cure receipt incompleteness — met its first full wave, and **zero of five items cleared jev-prewave**. Every build passed its own mechanical checks (harness assertions all PASS on all five final builds; A6 legs at 0 HITs on both legs for three items — T204 · T205 · T210 — with carried-with-disposition HITs on T199's fit leg and T208's census leg) and every HOLD was ASSERTED-CHECKS on receipt grounds (the returns' own checking basis varies and is qualified in §9b.4 — T204/T210 are paperwork reviews; T205's re-fire independently evaluated its CP01 predicate and found the build failing the written strict bound, a stronger finding than a missing receipt): T199 (two index lines claiming evidence that did not exist — a probe never run, a color never printed) · T204 (endpoint receipts + swap moved-instant receipts for five checkpoints + a fit row filed as a product instead of a measured bbox) · T205 (a strict-bound receipt failing at exactly 0.30 with no receipt at that instant · a fixed "8000ms" label in place of an evaluated instant · census rows overstating two phases' runtime effect) · T208 (timing-swap movement evidence for seven checkpoints via the inputs each assertion actually reads · a guard-#2 geometry receipt under content swap) · T210 (a hold-dependent swap probe · one stale index line printing a superseded value against its own receipt · CP9 without a whole-state equality receipt · palette swap without observed output values). Own-checks dimension moved with cure rounds (0.25→0.40 · 0.35→0.40/0.45/0.48 · T199 0.40→0.70 across cycles) but never crossed. The defect is no longer enumeration (A13's index exists on every item and reconciliations were performed) — it is **receipt validity at the margin**: receipts that are present, plausible, and one predicate short of what their assertion prescribes, plus index lines whose claims outrun their receipts. The judges catch these reliably; the builders' self-reconciliation did not. WHY the self-reconciliation missed them is **not established by this wave's evidence** — shared authorship (the same author writes the claim and checks it) is one hypothesis consistent with the filings, priced as a hypothesis in the candidate below, not as the pattern's cause.

**Candidate amendment (filed, NOT landed — priced for HQ): RECEIPT-INDEPENDENCE.** The A13 reconciliation gains a second pair of eyes: before the prewave payload is assembled, the receipt index is reconciled by a checker that did not author the build record — in this seat's form, a mechanical cross-check script where the assertion is mechanical (every CONFIG-expression receipt re-evaluated by script and diffed against the filed value; every claimed probe instant grepped in the filed raw output) plus the seat's spot re-probe of the index's highest-risk lines (swap receipts + endpoint receipts, the two classes named in three of this wave's five HOLDs). Evidence: 5 items, one wave, one defect class, against A13's own prediction (Cycle 036 §0b.1: the index "is priced to cut the re-fire count" — measured this wave: 9 prewave firings, 0 waves spent, 0 verdicts; the predicted re-fire reduction did not occur this wave, and with one wave and no clearance cohort, A13's effect on re-fire frequency remains unestablished rather than falsified). Landing form (instruction step · mechanical guard · Jev definition · Codex prompt) is HQ's pricing; this cycle files the candidate with its evidence and does not amend INSTRUCTION.md, because a second consecutive self-authored amendment to the same leg, landed the cycle after the first failed, is exactly the calibration-instead-of-pricing pattern the judgment-layer evaluation exists to catch. NOT-YET-AMENDED, consumer HQ.

**§0b dispositions:**
1. *T199 completion — DONE as charged, outcome NO VERDICT:* the authorized re-fire fired once, HOLDed on two overstated index lines (both judge-verified real; the builder recorded them as its own defects in scores.md). T199's further re-fire stands PENDING AUTHORIZATION (consumer HQ) under the Cycle-036 firing-3 reading — the NO-VERDICT pool awaiting authorization is now four items (T190 · T196 · T197 · T199), each with filed cures.
2. *T190/T196/T197 — UNCHANGED, PENDING AUTHORIZATION:* no authorization entry landed on this job's board this cycle (board re-read at Observe: 49 entries at open, last = wave33; the only new entry is this wave's own). The ask is NOT re-filed this cycle — it stands on the board from Wave 33 with consumer HQ; re-filing an identical ask every cycle is queue noise, and the four new items' completions (authorized under A12.3) are the next cycle's first charge regardless.
3. *Practice census-guard proposal — evidence INCOMPLETE, carried:* its consumer was a Condense with ≥3 scored items; this wave scored zero. Consumer re-named again: the next Condense with ≥3 scored items.
4. *Feed standard — FOLLOWED, one transport note:* every firing this cycle ran the standard form; all eight seat gate returns + all prewave returns arrived with verdict text duplicated after the token line (D-PAYLOAD-DUP, priced as one return each). The T205 builder's mid-Verify termination is recorded in §3 as a run-form failure (not a Plan defect): its filed work was consumed whole by the completion builder under A8, and no firing was repeated.
5. *Practice construction note (reserved-band badge treatment) — PRICED, first binding application:* T208's Phase A priced it BINDS (its ratio/population labels sit in reserved bands) and its builder applied it (population ink cured 9.4→11.6 px at 360 under the fit leg); T204/T205/T210 priced NOT-BINDING with reasons in their Phase A records. The note's receipt remains the HQ board entry until a scored item prices it.
6. *Wave-size / cadence re-price — UNASSESSED on measured cost (carried from Cycle 036):* per-item wall time still unmeasured; the interim cost unit (firings per scored item) is this wave UNDEFINED — 25 verdict-bearing or gate firings before Condense (Phase A 8 · seat gates 8 · prewave 9), 26 including this close's first condense call, produced 0 scored verdicts. The Cycle 036 comparator does not reconcile: its HQ entry reports 18 firings for 1 verdict, while its RUN's listed components yield 19 under this wave's counting convention (2 + 2 + 6 + 5 + 4), and the two cohorts differ in shape — the comparison is printed as unreconciled, not used as a rate. Wave size 5 and the standing cadence are CARRIED FORWARD PENDING EVIDENCE, not re-priced; the cost evidence that does stand is that prewave HOLDs blocked scoring on all five items — the call counts locate the stop; per-item wall time, cost share, and A13's effect on re-fire frequency remain unmeasured.

**Judgment-layer presence evaluation (standing, every Condense):** demanded judges, all hosted in this job's `guards/` and fired or consumed this cycle — codex-observe (×4 new items, Phase A) · codex-plan-review (×4, Phase A) · jev-observe-exit (×4) · jev-plan-exit (×4) · jev-prewave (fired on all 5 items: T199 ×1 authorized completion re-fire · new items ×2 each under the two-firing form) · A6 legs (×5 on final builds) · five-lens scoring wave (NOT fired — no item earned it; the non-firing is the two-HOLD rule working, printed as such) · codex-condense (fired at this close, record below).
- *Instruction steps:* NO amendment landed this cycle — the RECEIPT-INDEPENDENCE candidate is filed above as NOT-YET-AMENDED with consumer HQ and its reason (a self-authored second amendment to the same leg, the cycle after the first did not produce its predicted effect, is not priced as a cure until the independence question is answered). A13 stands as landed; its predicted re-fire reduction did not occur this wave and its effect remains unestablished (§9b.5).
- *Mechanical guards:* guards.md priced per command — commands 1/2/3/5/6/7 each produced their filed outputs on all five items and no HOLD named a guard-text defect; command 8 (census-anchor probes) was the evidentiary basis of two T210/T205 cure items — text NO-DEFECT. The gap the wave exposes is not a command's text but the absence of an independent re-evaluation step over filed receipts — that absence is the candidate above, owned by HQ's pricing, not silently cured here.
- *Jev definitions:* jev-prewave — NO-DEFECT, positively demonstrated: across 9 firings it caught receipt defects on five consecutive builds on the checking bases its returns state (paperwork review for T204/T210 · independent predicate evaluation for T205's finding 1 · harness re-run for T205's cure confirmations), confirmed cures landed where they had (T205 firing 2 · T199's cure credit), and never passed a record whose receipts were short; the failure sits in the records fed to it, not its definition. jev-observe-exit — NO-DEFECT with two priced open questions (§9b.3): its T204 RETURN (mechanics 0.5, all else 1.0) priced missing continuous-motion evidence; the Execute-open receipt form filed frame-sequence records, not playback, on both occasions it was used (T199 Wave 33 · T204 Wave 34), so the RETURN class is NOT cured by that form and the earlier "worked / twice-demonstrated" reading is withdrawn — the seat's §1.2 playback debt stands NOT-YET-AMENDED, consumer the next Condense, priced together with (i) the §5 floor basis at exactly 0.5 and (ii) the FED-list receipt-form question, all three in the same call file. jev-plan-exit — NO-DEFECT: four REVISEs, every charge verified real by the builders' amendments (T208's cascade arithmetic — the gate's 6930 ms vs the Plan's 5430 ms — caught a schedule error that would have cost the verdict; T205's return caught the split-view geometry/count contradiction — which columns the split view could show — while WHICH side is visible was resolved later by the completion builder's D1 census finding, and is not credited to the gate).
- *Codex prompts:* codex-observe — NO-DEFECT (finding pairs: T205's defective evidence frame + window overstatement, both confirmed firsthand and cured in the record · T210's T54 baseline correction). codex-plan-review — NO-DEFECT, with a named finding pair: its T208 firing priced the ratio-rounding defect (701,888.89 filed without a rounding rule) and the Plan adopted `ratioRounding:1000` in consequence — a finding-and-treatment pair on the filed record (`item-T208-codex-plan-review-return.md` + the item record's §P9 amendments); the remaining three items' REVISE findings were likewise applied in their Phase A records before the gates. codex-scoring-wave — NOT DEMANDED this cycle (no FIRE-WAVE); its definition stands unamended. codex-condense — NO-DEFECT for its definition: firing 1's REVISE produced exactly the corrections §9b carries (evidence qualification · per-command dispositions · the RETURN re-disposition · exact return paths · cost reconciliation) and firing 2's REVISE produced the operative-text corrections that follow it; a definition whose checks force their own cycle's cures is working as designed, and no text change to it is proposed.
- **JUDGMENT LAYER: COMPLETE** — all demanded judges hosted + current as disposed above; the print is final only with a filed codex-condense ACCEPT covering this corrected §9 (firing record below).

**§9b — codex-condense firing 1 dispositions (REVISE, applied in full):**
1. *Candidate's causal claim corrected:* the §9 pattern's "same author writes the claim and checks it" is **consistent with the evidence, not established by it** — Wave 34 establishes that builder readiness checks let deficient receipts reach jev-prewave on all five items; it does not establish shared authorship as the cause or independence as the cure. The candidate stands NOT-YET-AMENDED with consumer HQ, its owning surfaces named: INSTRUCTION.md §5 leg 3b (the readiness step) + the mechanical guard layer (guards.md). **Acceptance test for HQ, from the filed failures:** any landed form must catch, on the filed Wave-34 records, (a) T199's A-8 — the exact probe and window a receipt claims must exist in the filed raw output (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-completion2.md`, findings 1–2); (b) T199's B-17 — an observed swapped color must be printed by the swap receipt it is claimed under (same return); (c) T205's CP01 class — a binding predicate evaluated AT its endpoint (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, finding 1: `stateAt(570 ms)` = exactly 0.30 against a strict < 0.30 bound). A grep-for-instant + CONFIG-diff check alone would miss (b) and (c) — the test says so on its face. The handoff's board state: HQ.json still carries this wave's Plan skeleton at firing time; the closed entry (§10 filings) is the handoff's confirmation.
2. *Mechanical guards, complete disposition:* command 4 (scores arithmetic) — **NOT DEMANDED this cycle** (no lens scores exist to consolidate; its non-firing is the two-HOLD rule's consequence, not an omission). Commands 2/6/7 — their REQUIREMENTS are sound; three FILED OUTPUTS were deficient, which supports deferring a receipt-validation change to HQ rather than amending guard text here: command 2 (swap) — T208's re-fire found no regenerated-geometry result under content swap (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T208-paired-dot-counts-house-stage/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`) · command 6 (fit leg) — T204's swap-title fit row lacked a measured post-fit width (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T204-dot-grid-identity-withheld-title/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`) · command 7 (census leg) — T205's census overstated two phases' runtime application (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, finding 3). Merely producing an output does not prove the guard was satisfied — §9's earlier per-command line stands corrected to this form. **Command 8 (census-anchor probes)** — its requirement (raw stateAt probes at the census anchors) is sound and T199's completion re-fire expressly identifies its A-8 finding as a command-8 receipt failure: the earliest filed state dump sits at 800 ms, outside the plate-owned window [0,800) the index line claimed (same T199 return, finding 1). The command's text needs no change; VALIDATION of its filed outputs is part of the HQ deferral in §9b.1.
3. *Motion evidence + the observe-exit RETURN, re-disposed:* the T204 builder's receipt (32 frames inspected in sequence at 4 fps + two source stills) is **not** the continuous playback the gate requested, and T205's record likewise carries decoded-frame probes, not playback. The §2b disposition is therefore corrected: jev-observe-exit's T204 **RETURN-TO-OBSERVE is recorded as SET ASIDE with the gap carried** (the wave proceeded on census-proven mechanics; the playback evidence the call requires was never produced, and the gap is a standing Observe debt of this seat, named here rather than cured by relabeling). Two rule questions are priced for the call file's next Condense, NOT-YET-AMENDED with this reason: (i) the gate's §5 floor fires RETURN at any dimension **< 0.5**, and T204's mechanics scored exactly **0.5** — the RETURN therefore rests on the MECHANICS-UNSEEN taxonomy judgment, not the floor; whether a 0.5 mechanics score with complete frame evidence should RETURN is an unresolved rule question the return itself does not cite a basis for; (ii) the FED-list receipt-form change (§9's jev-observe-exit candidate) is deferred to the SAME Condense that prices (i) — both edits live in one call file, and piecemeal single-cycle edits to one call file are the divergence pattern this job has retired before. codex-observe's scope is the source-record audit (packet completeness · prior-attempt record · segment facts) — continuous-motion verification is the seat's §1.2 act, not that prompt's charge; the missed playback evidence is disposed as the seat's Observe defect above, not a codex-observe miss. Its NO-DEFECT line stands on that basis.
4. *Evidence binding (exact return paths):* T199 cross-cycle delta — prior re-fire `hidden_files/study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md` (0.75/1.00/0.40/0.75) → completion re-fire `…/codex/jev-prewave-completion2.md` (0.90/1.00/0.70/0.90). T204 — `hidden_files/study/recreations/T204-dot-grid-identity-withheld-title/codex/jev-prewave.md` → `…/jev-prewave-refire.md`. T205 — `hidden_files/study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave.md` → `…/jev-prewave-refire.md`. T208 — `hidden_files/study/recreations/T208-paired-dot-counts-house-stage/codex/jev-prewave.md` → `…/jev-prewave-refire.md`. T210 — `hidden_files/study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/codex/jev-prewave.md` → `…/jev-prewave-refire.md`. "Judges verified as real" in §9's pattern paragraph is qualified per §9b's head correction: each HOLD's grounds were checked on the basis its return states (paperwork review for T204/T210; independent predicate evaluation for T205's finding 1; harness re-run for T205's cure confirmations).
5. *Cost accounting corrected:* 25 firings before Condense (8 + 8 + 9), 26 including firing 1 of this close — §9 disposition 6 stands as corrected in place. A13's first full wave produced zero clearances; its effect on re-fire frequency remains **unestablished** (one wave, no clearance cohort to compare) — the stronger claim in §9's candidate paragraph ("the prediction failed on its first test") is retained only in its narrow form: the predicted re-fire reduction did not occur this wave (9 prewave firings, 5 of them re-fires or completion re-fires, 0 waves spent).

