40:- Disposition: the verdict is advisory — reviewed by the runner, applied or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense. The verdict + classification + disposition land in the build record either way; an applied HOLD leaves the item IN PROGRESS and the wave moves to its next item (a held item never holds the wave hostage).
../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave.md
18:- Deliverable: an attempt's build record (parameter table · construction route · own-checks results) BEFORE the Codex wave fires.
19:- Call point: recreation INSTRUCTION §4, between the builder's own checks (§5.2) and the wave (§5.3). The verdict is advisory: applied, a HOLD returns the build to the builder with named defects and the wave does not fire on that item; set aside, the miss is recorded in Condense. An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
22:Judge whether this build record shows a recreation ready to be scored, or one whose defects are already visible in its own paperwork. Price: (1) PARAMETERIZATION — is the piece genuinely CONFIG-driven (fields named, ranges sane), or hard-coded with a config costume? (2) PURITY PRE-CHECK — does the construction route describe generation from parameters, with no tracing/embedding step hiding in the prose? (3) OWN-CHECKS COMPLETENESS — are the mechanical guards' results recorded (purity grep, swap test, syntax), or asserted? **Census-checkpoint mapping (Amendment A11, landed 2026-11-17, Cycle 028 Condense): every Observe census checkpoint for the item must map to an executable own-check assertion whose evaluation instant is CONFIG-derived; the build-record identifies checkpoint · assertion · CONFIG expression · evaluated result. ASSERTED-CHECKS is returned if any checkpoint lacks this mapping, any evaluation instant uses hardcoded defaults, or execution evidence is absent; a CONFIG timing swap must be shown to move the corresponding assertion's evaluation instant. Receipt form (Amendment A12, landed 2026-11-18, Cycle 035 Condense): the execution evidence for each assertion is its EXECUTABLE RECEIPT — harness command or run · CONFIG expression evaluated · raw result from the build under review (for a timing swap, the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant); a claim without its receipt is execution evidence absent. **Receipt-index ground (Amendment A13, landed 2026-11-18, Cycle 036 Condense): a build-record whose RECEIPT INDEX (INSTRUCTION A13.1) is missing an expected entry (an applicable guards.md command, a planned A11 assertion, an assertion inherited whole from a prior attempt's filed harness, or a census row for an expected CONFIG key), carries an exclusion whose disposition cites no governing plan or guard, or carries a populated receipt lacking the evidence its assertion requires (CONFIG expression + evaluated value for CONFIG-derived inputs; raw observed result for checks) is an ASSERTED-CHECKS ground by name.** The same leg prices the A6 fit evidence: a fit-table row lacking measurement provenance, or carrying model-derived bounds, per guard-measured-fit.md checks 1–2 is an ASSERTED-CHECKS ground.** (4) TECHNIQUE FIDELITY PLAN — does the record state which packet mechanics the build implements and which it deliberately defers (a deferral named is lawful; a mechanic silently absent is not)? Score 0–1 per dimension, classify defects. You judge paperwork only: a build can pass you and still fail its wave — your job is that no wave is spent on a build its own record already condemns.
25:- FED: build-record.md · the CONFIG block of recreation.html · the technique's packet section · guards.md command list (what own-checks should exist) · **the item's A6 leg outputs (fit-table.md + config-census.md) — added 2026-11-16, recreation Cycle 024 Condense, on the Wave-21 pattern: prewave firings for T151, T153 and T154 all HOLDed or re-fired on feed completeness (the A6 files and packet section existed complete in the artifact directory but were not in the payload), the lane's recurring ASSERTED-CHECKS false-positive class. A payload lacking any FED element is a feeder defect, printed as such in the build record; a HOLD whose only named cure is feeding an already-filed FED element is disposed as a feed-completeness miss, with the miss recorded.**
26:- FED (added 2026-11-17, Cycle 026 Condense — the T167 miss): **the wave record's binding census-anchor mapping for the item + any Observe dispositions pricing source ambiguities** (the §1d-form: where a packet caption or digest line admits two readings, the wave record's priced reading governs). A HOLD founded on a source ambiguity the wave record has already priced is a feeder defect, disposed as such in the build record — the judge prices the build against the binding mapping, not against raw source prose. (Founding miss: Cycle 026 T167 — HOLD priced a packet caption's ambiguous reading against a build that followed the gate-approved mapping; the seat upheld the set-aside at §5.)
31:- Verdict classes: **FIRE-WAVE · HOLD**.
32:- Dimensions (0–1): parameterization · purity pre-check · own-checks completeness · fidelity-plan honesty.
34:- Accepted profile travels: cited in scores.md's pre-wave line; a wave fired over a HOLD is a deviation (WAVE-OVER-HOLD).
37:- Any dimension < 0.5 → HOLD · ASSERTED-CHECKS at any score on other dimensions → HOLD (unrecorded checks are the lane's named failure class).
38:- Disposition: the verdict is advisory — reviewed by the runner, applied or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense. The verdict + classification + disposition land in the build record either way; an applied HOLD leaves the item IN PROGRESS and the wave moves to its next item (a held item never holds the wave hostage).
44:- Exemplars: T15 attempt 1's build record (must FIRE-WAVE: checks recorded, deferral of the interlude named in its Plan) · a constructed record claiming a swap test with no harness output (must HOLD as ASSERTED-CHECKS) · a constructed record whose CONFIG is decorative over hard-coded phrases (must HOLD as HARDCODED-CONFIG).
