../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/plan-amendment-cycle037-addendum1.md:11:**Disposition (governs):** the split view shows the lattice from its WESTERN edge — first visible column = **0** — translated right so the disc + connector gap stand at the left; columns are cropped at the stage's RIGHT edge. The converting block is `west` (colRange [0,4]) and it IS the visible, washed block in the split view. Cure 8's `layout.splitFirstVisibleCol = 15` / "columns 15–33 visible" disposition is **SUPERSEDED AND RETIRED**: it priced the crop on the wrong side (it would have hidden the converting block entirely). Plan §2.1's original "showing the western blocks" reading is the governing one.
../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/plan-amendment-cycle037-addendum1.md:12:**Geometry bound (CONFIG):** split grid left edge = disc centre + disc radius + connector gap = `geom.discCenterXPx (190) + geom.discDiameterPx/2 (170) + geom.connectorGapPx (160, NEW key) = 520` design px (census proportion: connector spans ≈160/960 of stage width in the 44.0 s frame). New pure helpers in the build — `fullGridX/fullGridY`, `splitGridX`, `visibleCellStats`, `washVisibility`, `connectorGeometry` — are the SAME functions the renderer uses for its split translation and connector target, so harness receipts over them ARE renderer receipts, not state-model arithmetic. Expected split counts under this geometry (pitch 24, cell 14): columns 0–18 intersect the 960 px stage (**342 cells intersecting** — the number 342 survives, its derivation does not: it is 19 intersecting columns × 18, not (34−15)×18), columns 0–17 fully within (**324 cells**), column 18 partial at the right edge. `layout.splitFirstVisibleCol` and `geom.splitRightMarginPx` are REMOVED from CONFIG (their only sites were the superseded formula); the removal + replacement is reconciled in config-census.md.
../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/plan-amendment-cycle037-addendum1.md:13:**Mirror layout (disc-right):** the split geometry mirrors about the stage centre — grid right edge at 960 − 520 = 440, grid left edge at 440 − 806 = −366; visible columns are the eastern ones (16–33 fully within, 15 partial), and the mirror exercise's changed partition (`east`, colRange [29,33]) is the visible/washed block there. Connector target in mirror = the grid's right edge (440); contact difference must be 0 at connectorProgress = 1 in both layouts.
