# Codex review — codex-condense (recreation)

_Repeated Codex review type, defined in this job's own guards layer (phase-guard augmentation, 2026-11-14). Execution: Codex via the fleet feeding rule (one stream); the DEFINITION lives here._

## Standing header (every run opens with it)
1. **Consumer:** recreation's §9 Condense for the closing cycle + the decision priced: whether the cycle's lessons were faithfully encoded into the instruction layer (steps · mechanical guards · Jev definitions · Codex prompts), or whether an amendment claims a lesson its text does not carry.
2. **Working record:** the cycle's RUN.md (traces + returns) + INSTRUCTION.md as amended this Condense + guards/ as amended this Condense + verdict-history.md — the run builds from the cycle record and the amended files, and writes its return into the cycle record's Condense section.
3. **Body-write:** the return must end with a `BODY-WRITE:` line naming what it filed; a read-only run closes with "Body-write: none (read-only run)" and the consumer (the cycle record) persists the return verbatim.

## The review
Fires at §9 Condense close, after the cycle's amendments are drafted and before the cycle record closes. The run attacks:
- **Faithfulness of each amendment:** for every lesson promoted this cycle (dated, technique cited — §9 form), does the amended instruction/guard text actually encode the lesson such that a cold builder following only the text would behave differently? An amendment that names a cure in prose while leaving the operative step unchanged is classified AMENDMENT-THEATRE. Founding calibration shape: Amendment A5 — Owner Cures 1+2 landed as construction requirements AND a fifth lens in §5.4 AND flow-field guidance; a lesser encoding (a mention in a lessons list) would have failed this attack.
- **Four-layer coverage:** did this cycle's experience touch each layer — (1) instruction steps, (2) mechanical guard code/commands (guards.md), (3) Jev definitions (jev-prewave · jev-observe-exit · jev-plan-exit), (4) Codex prompts (codex-scoring-wave · codex-observe · codex-plan-review · this file) — and for each untouched layer, is the no-change a NO-DEFECT proof naming the evidence checked, or an escape? A reversed verdict, a defect that passed a gate, or a lens finding that recurred across two techniques (§9 pattern rule) MUST land on its owning layer or be named not-yet-amended with reason (the presence-evaluation rule).
- **Score-evidence binding:** every lesson citing a lens score cites the filed return (artifact codex/ path); a lesson priced from the seat's summary rather than the return is named.
- **Wave re-pricing honesty (§0):** if this cycle re-priced wave size or cadence, the return checks the re-price cites measured per-item cost from THIS cycle's filings — a re-price from expectation is attacked.
The run does not re-score recreations and does not edit files; its REVISE verdict returns the named amendment to Condense for re-encoding before the cycle closes.

## Feeding contract
- ONE stream: this instruction + the cycle's RUN.md + the amendment diffs drafted this Condense (before/after text) + the §9 candidate-lesson list — never pipe + stdin together (fleet rule).
- One run per cycle (not per item): the consumer is the job's next cycle, which inherits the amended layer only after this review's verdict is filed.

## Demonstration / firing state
- **DEFINED** (2026-11-14). **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** No run has fired under this definition; Cycles 001–002 Condensed without it (their amendments A1–A5 stand as filed; this review prices future Condenses, it does not retro-judge them). First demonstration: the next recreation wave's Condense.

codex
**REVISE — the RECEIPT-INDEPENDENCE deferral is faithful. The draft still overstates the mechanical and Jev findings, misattributes a Codex finding, and leaves the HQ handoff unconfirmed.**

1. **Keep RECEIPT-INDEPENDENCE as NOT-YET-AMENDED.** `INSTRUCTION.md` §5 leg 3b and A13 already require valid evidence. Wave 34 shows that the builder readiness checks let deficient receipts through. Shared authorship remains a hypothesis. `RUN.md` §9b.1 gives HQ a concrete test for any proposed change: catch T199’s missing in-window state dump and missing observed swap color, and reject T205’s `0.30` at 570 ms under a strict `< 0.30` bound. The current `HQ.json` entry `rec-2026-11-18-wave34` still says PLANNED and carries no candidate. Preserve the disposition and record the handoff as pending until the board entry confirms it. [T199 completion return, findings 1–2](../../../../study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-completion2.md) · [T205 re-fire return, finding 1](../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md) · [HQ.json](../../HQ.json#L404)

2. **Put the mechanical guard dispositions in the operative §9 bullet.** It still cites production of outputs as support for NO-DEFECT, while §9b.2 records deficient outputs under commands 2, 6, 7, and 8. State which requirements were checked, which outputs fell short, and which validation work is deferred to HQ. Command 4 was not demanded because there were no lens scores. Also qualify §9b.2’s command 8 wording. The guard requires a raw probe at a named empty or zero-state anchor. T199’s A-8 additionally claimed a dump inside `[0,800)`, and the filed return found the earliest dump at 800 ms. [RUN.md, §9 and §9b.2](RUN.md#L87) · [guards.md, commands 1–8](../../guards/guards.md)

3. **Scope the Jev proof to what the returns checked, and reconcile the playback record.** The nine prewave calls all issued HOLDs on the records supplied. That supports the named dispositions. The claim that Jev “never passed a record whose receipts were short” reaches beyond this cohort. T199’s return expressly limits itself to fed paperwork, so §9 should describe A-8 as a missing filed dump and B-17 as a missing observed color in the named receipt. T205’s endpoint failure has independent evaluation behind it. For Observe exit, `RUN.md` §2b correctly sets aside T204’s RETURN and carries the playback gap, but T204’s plan amendment A4 and its closing charge summary still claim a playback cure. A dated supersession would make the artifact agree with the operative disposition. The `< 0.5` floor and the separate MECHANICS-UNSEEN judgment can remain deferred together as recorded. [RUN.md, §2b and §9b.3](RUN.md#L43) · [T204 plan amendment, A4](../../../../study/recreations/T204-dot-grid-identity-withheld-title/plan-amendment-cycle037.md#L32) · [Jev Observe exit, §§2 and 5](../../guards/jev-observe-exit.md)

4. **Replace the Codex Plan-review finding pair.** T208’s nearest-thousand rounding came from **codex-observe** and was adopted in §P1 before Plan review. The Plan-review file repeats it in the input. Its actual finding 3 asked for `cascadeMs` to own the landing window and for one- and three-column swap fixtures. T208 §P9 R3 records both changes and is a valid finding-and-treatment pair. The Codex scoring-wave disposition is supported because no item reached FIRE-WAVE. [T208 Observe/Plan, §P1 and §P9 R3](item-T208-observe-plan.md#L139) · [T208 Codex Plan-review return](item-T208-codex-plan-review-return.md)

5. **Score binding and wave re-pricing pass with one wording correction.** §9b.4 points to the filed prewave returns for the own-checks deltas. These are Jev readiness dimensions. There were zero five-lens scores. The count reconciles as 8 Phase A calls + 8 seat gates + 9 prewave calls = **25 before Condense**. With zero scored items, firings per scored item is undefined. Carrying wave size and cadence forward pending measured cost is faithful to §0. Replace “the predicted re-fire reduction did not occur” with the observed result: four first attempts each used a re-fire, T199 used its carried completion re-fire, and none cleared. The size of any A13 effect remains unestablished. [RUN.md, §9 disposition 6 and §9b.4–5](RUN.md#L85) · [INSTRUCTION.md, §0](../../INSTRUCTION.md#L10)

**Limits:** This was a review of the filed records and returns. I did not re-run the harnesses, assess source playback, or verify a closed HQ entry. The on-disk verdict history ends at Cycle 036, so Wave 34’s history filing remains unverified. [verdict-history.md](../../verdict-history.md)

